  "body": "Implements Accepted ADR 0031 I6-B R02–R09, stacked directly on #149. The v5-only strict codec preserves canonical seven-column Resource identification, complete original Parent and endpoint references, generic report/terminal alternatives, Source and original Coverage evidence. The pure finite dependency planner selects or withholds whole semantic units with cumulative actual-work accounting.\n\nI6-A service-bound current authority, replay revalidation, both exact SQL Transfer fences and unconnected Provider/Exchange refusal remain in force. I6-C/I7/I8 and normal Transfer activation are deferred. No #139/#142/#144/#147 implementation is imported. Task B #150 remains a separate audit.\n\nAuthor validation:\n\n- Complete ordinary snapshot `2f874ce`: 6,288 unique nodes, 5,987 PASS / 281 FAIL / 20 ERROR; all 212 new nodes pass. Two old three-column guard fixtures are migrated with every other test statement and all four assertion ASTs unchanged.\n- Final source `a354348`: safety 626 (I4 217 / I5 29 included), wire/planner 212 and external 34 PASS. Matched 745 diagnostics: 446 PASS / 279 FAIL / 20 ERROR; the two guards recover and the historical 299-node unsuccessful set remains. One inherited I6-C malformed-input refusal moves earlier; full node/type/code/assertion mappings are retained.\n- Each independent direct-wheel / sdist-wheel environment: safety 626, wire 212, external 34, reused authorization 27 and reused Task C 132 PASS, plus original/fence controls. Actual imports, 160 product files / 6,022,477 bytes, archive and installed RECORD, full source/sdist retention, schema/UDF/integrity and both fences verify.\n- Original Access smoke actually FAILS at unconnected export in each minimal artifact environment, exit 1; subsequent steps are unexecuted. Earlier jsonschema-missing collection exit 4 is separately preserved.\n\nThe final-commit complete ordinary suite is **UNEXECUTED** after the fixture-only migration. The entire product tree matches the completed `2f874ce` run; no aggregate is reconstructed from overlapping lanes. Live/benchmark opt-ins, independent non-Author I6-B review and complete Release acceptance are unexecuted.\n\n[Author report](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/ef787a5ff8b13f118d6bf5107c7338f43fde56dc/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6b-author-20261023/REPORT.md) · [R/V/T matrix](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/ef787a5ff8b13f118d6bf5107c7338f43fde56dc/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6b-author-20261023/MATRIX.md) · [Complete artifact inventory](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/blob/ef787a5ff8b13f118d6bf5107c7338f43fde56dc/docs/implementation/evidence/adr0031-i6b-author-20261023/ARTIFACTS.json). Commands, process exits, source/input hashes, JUnit/journals, failed/interrupted/parser-control attempts and all byte/origin/RECORD inventories are retained.\n\nPublication HEAD `ef787a5ff8b13f118d6bf5107c7338f43fde56dc`, tree `a3ed2628a98db134bdc65d13da905f5ddf25e972`. Execution/build source `a354348b800177608f6a83e2484cb6a784b7190a`, tree `169f0f95449c7bd728261b3d7799f795162c03fd`; all 484 executed inputs match publication, whose follow-up changes evidence only. Full publication sdist bytes were not rebuilt.\n\nFinal-HEAD [Development CI run 39955068751](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39955068751) is **SUCCESS**: both `offline` and `sqlite-policy` pass. Actual in-log indexed receipt SHA-256 `7622c0d22dac39585c968ebfd04cc8a7667c64500dcbe3b964d1d005d5255c4e` (92,059 bytes) verifies feature HEAD, checkout `54464ad882ee644ff37f0af0a3a8d5af52f9f7ec`, effective tree, run/attempt and every payload hash. The actual merge has ordered parents base `ea43a21` / feature `ef787a5`, and its tree equals the feature tree.\n\nManifest: `acceptance_status=development_checks_passed`, `full_acceptance=false`, 0 hosted product-pytest cases; 31 policy + 4 runtime-binding stdlib tests pass. Hosted product Python is 3.12.15 using its actual SQLite 3.53.1. `evidence_status=local_evidence_unavailable` means this generic CI did not ingest the custom Author receipts linked above; it does not turn them into hosted runtime acceptance.\n\nThe additional automatically triggered [Access registry CI 39955068823](https://github.com/TakashiSasaki/git-repo-db/actions/runs/39955068823) is still **IN PROGRESS** at this Author status snapshot; its broad legacy runtime/artifact checks are not included in the Development success claim. Development CI Success is separate from complete Release acceptance. This is an Author submission; the parent requests the non-Author review next. No merge, release or deployment is requested.\n",
